Found by reading Proxy.pm (2026-09-29), not reproduced yet.

_inject_node_auth_async (lib/Langertha/Skeid/Proxy.pm) leaves the client's Authorization header untouched when neither the KeyBroker nor api_key_env yields a key. That is the documented pass-through for a node with NO key of its own. It also happens for a node that HAS api_key_ref / api_key_env configured but whose key cannot be resolved: broker error, cached failure, empty env var. And build_app only warns when the OpenBao login fails at boot and runs without a broker -- then has_key_broker is false and every api_key_ref node takes the pass-through branch.

Result: the customer's Skeid key is sent to the upstream provider as Bearer token (ADR 0003 in spirit: a secret reaches a party that must never see it).

Wanted: a node with a configured key source (api_key_ref or api_key_env) that resolves to nothing fails closed -- no upstream call, error in the face's own shape (502/503), request.finish with ok => 0, one usage event, the reference in the log but never a key. A node with neither keeps the pass-through. t/22-key-broker.t covers only the env-fallback case today.

Reproduce first (red test), then fix.

